slice("abc", start: 0, len: 1)
---
error[Z0401]: `start:` of `slice` counts positions from 1, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:21
  |
1 | slice("abc", start: 0, len: 1)
  |                     ^ before the first character
  |
  = help: the first character is at position 1, as in R's `substr` and Stata's `substr`

slice("abc", start: 1, len: -1)
---
error[Z0401]: `len:` of `slice` is a number of characters, but this is -1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:29
  |
1 | slice("abc", start: 1, len: -1)
  |                             ^^ a negative length
  |
  = help: `len: 0` gives the empty text; a length past the end gives what is there

slice("abc", start: 1)
---
error[Z0406]: `slice` needs `len:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | slice("abc", start: 1)
  | ^^^^^ `len:` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `slice(s, start: 1, len: 3)` for the first three characters

pad("abc")
---
error[Z0406]: `pad` needs `width:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | pad("abc")
  | ^^^ `width:` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `pad(s, width: 8)` for eight characters, spaces on the left

pad("abc", width: -1)
---
error[Z0401]: `width:` of `pad` is a number of characters, but this is -1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | pad("abc", width: -1)
  |                   ^^ a negative width
  |
  = help: a width below the text's length leaves the text as it is

pad("abc", width: 5, fill: "ab")
---
error[Z0401]: `fill:` of `pad` is one character, but this is 2 characters
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:28
  |
1 | pad("abc", width: 5, fill: "ab")
  |                            ^^^^ not one character
  |
  = help: `fill: "0"` pads a number with zeros, `fill: "."` leads the eye across a table

pad("abc", width: 5, fill: "")
---
error[Z0401]: `fill:` of `pad` is one character, but this is empty
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:28
  |
1 | pad("abc", width: 5, fill: "")
  |                            ^^ not one character
  |
  = help: `fill: "0"` pads a number with zeros, `fill: "."` leads the eye across a table

